          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is egg white protein good for weight loss?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can fit a weight-loss diet well, because it is almost pure protein, with no fat and very little carbohydrate, at roughly 110 calories per 25 g of protein. Protein helps with fullness and preserving muscle while you eat less. It is not special for fat loss, though; total calories and total protein across the day matter more than the source."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who should not use egg white protein?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Anyone with an egg allergy should avoid it. People with kidney disease, those who are pregnant, and anyone taking medication should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before adding a protein supplement. People watching sodium for blood pressure should count the few hundred milligrams in each serving."
