      <a href="#top-picks">Our Top Picks</a>
      <a href="#what-it-is">What Egg White Protein Is</a>
      <a href="#egg-vs-whey-plant">Egg vs Whey vs Plant</a>
      <a href="#biotin-avidin">Biotin and Avidin</a>
      <a href="#allergy">Egg Allergy and Safety</a>
      <a href="#downsides">Sodium, Foam and Taste</a>
      <a href="#how-we-picked">How We Picked</a>
      <a href="#how-to-use">How to Use It</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Egg white protein powder is the best choice for people who want a complete, animal-based protein without dairy. It has no lactose, no fat, a high-quality amino acid profile and none of the legume issues some people have with pea. It costs more per gram than whey, tastes plain, carries a fair amount of natural sodium and can foam in a shaker. For most buyers, Naked Egg is the best single-ingredient option, NOW Sports is the budget pick, and Jay Robb is the one to try if you want a flavored shake.
        </p>

