          <p>
            On quality, egg white protein is close to the top. It scores at the maximum on the PDCAAS scale used to rank protein quality, it contains all nine essential amino acids in good proportions, and it is highly digestible once cooked or pasteurized. Whey scores as well or better, and its higher leucine content is the main reason it is the default for muscle building. Leucine is the amino acid most closely tied to switching on muscle protein synthesis.
          </p>

